    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st quarter",
        "score": "CHI 10, NE 0",
        "text": "Cairo Santos' 43-yard field goal and D'Andre Swift's 4-yard touchdown run with 1:38 left gave Chicago a 10–0 lead after one."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd quarter",
        "score": "CHI 20, NE 14",
        "text": "Drake Maye's 7-yard touchdown run made it 10–7 with 11:33 left in the half, and a Santos field goal made it 13–7. Linebacker D'Marco Jackson intercepted Maye's deep pass for rookie tight end Eli Raridon, and Luther Burden III took a screen 24 yards for a touchdown on third-and-17 with 14 seconds left (20–7). On the last play of the half, Maye lobbed a pass over Cam Lewis to Rhamondre Stevenson, who went 48 yards for a touchdown."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd quarter",
        "score": "CHI 27, NE 21",
        "text": "Caleb Williams' 12-yard touchdown pass to Colston Loveland made it 27–14, and Maye answered with a 30-yard touchdown pass to Raridon with 3:46 left in the quarter (27–21). Bears cornerback Malik Muhammad left with a toe injury."
      },
      {
        "label": "4th quarter",
        "score": "Final: CHI 30, NE 24",
        "text": "Santos missed a 53-yarder early in the quarter, then hit a career-long 58-yard field goal, matching the franchise record, for a 30–21 lead with 1:34 left. Maye drove New England into range for Andy Borregales' 47-yard field goal with 37 seconds left, but Chicago recovered the onside kick."
      }
    ],
